  "notes": [
    "All six already-defined SD host/card signal mappings are preserved. No switch from four-wire to one-wire operation is made here.",
    "R710-R715 visibly connect to actual TMUX source pins; their opposite terminals use the original SD host nets.",
    "Native J701 pin9=SD_DETECT_CONTACT, pin11=GND, pins10/12/13/14=shell GND. Their numbers are not assumed to match the old library.",
    "U706 pins8,9,11,12 remain NC; select pins10,13 are tied to local GND.",
    "R701-R705 pull up CMD/D0-D3 to SD_3V3; R706 pulls CLK down to GND.",
    "R708 and C704 form visible contact-to-detect filtering; U705.1 stays on contact side and U705.2 protects SD_3V3.",
    "MCU/card inter-block nets use short native labels; ESD array inputs share card-side names. Global grounds are never drawn through unrelated blocks.",
    "Series resistor labels are near 10-unit-pitch chip lanes: root must visually place their Designator/Name attributes in the free gutter beside the short pin-net labels after native export."
  ]
}
